AN  - 32232951
AB  - Cytomegalovirus (CMV) is a DNA virus of the Herpesviridae family and is estimated to affect 15%‐30% of high‐risk solid organ transplant recipients. Typical manifestations of CMV end‐organ disease in this population include colitis, esophagitis, and pneumonitis, and myocarditis is a rarely reported manifestation. We describe two cases of CMV myocarditis in solid organ transplant recipients and review the literature regarding previously published cases of CMV myocarditis.
